.TH KLVTOOL-UPDATE 1 "1970-01-01" "klvtool dev" "User Commands"
.SH "NAME"
klvtool\-update \- Update klvtool to the latest GitHub release.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
klvtool update [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-prefer\-binary]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Update the running klvtool binary to the latest release tagged on GitHub. By default, prefer `go install` when go is on PATH (faster, no archive extraction). Use \-\-prefer\-binary to force the release\-archive path. Update is skipped on dev builds.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
print the chosen install strategy without acting
.TP
\fB\-\-prefer\-binary\fR
download the release archive even if go is on PATH
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Update in place
.RS 4
.nf
$ klvtool update
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show what would happen without acting
.RS 4
.nf
$ klvtool update --dry-run
.fi
.RE
.PP
Force the release\-archive path
.RS 4
.nf
$ klvtool update --prefer-binary
.fi
.RE
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
success or already up to date
.TP
\fB1\fR
release lookup failed, install failed, or write to install path failed
.TP
\fB2\fR
invalid usage
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBklvtool\fR(1),
\fBklvtool\-version\fR(1)
